he \"recupero\" (recovery).\n       Drafting thought:* Mention the cost. Rerouting a whole delegation (players, staff, medical team, equipment) via alternative routes (likely through Europe or Asia) is an unbudgeted expense for the Iranian Federation.\n       Drafting thought:* Avoid \"scandalo\". Focus on the \"fallimento dei protocolli di accoglienza\" (failure of welcome protocols).\n\n       Opening:* Focus on the logistical breakdown. The denial of visas for the staff is a technical failure in the pre-tournament coordination.\n       Middle:* Discuss the \"acclimatamento\" (acclimatization) issue. For a professional athlete, a 12-hour time difference combined with a disrupted travel schedule isn't a minor inconvenience; it's a physiological risk. The \"ritardo\" (delay) isn't just a clock issue; it's a biological one.\n       Deeper context:* The geopolitical tension between the US and Iran is being leveraged in a space—the World Cup—where FIFA usually demands neutrality to protect its commercial interests. However, the \"scalo a Washington\" failure proves that the commercial/sporting bubble is porous.\n       Closing:* A professional evaluation. If the Iranian staff cannot stabilize their routine due to these logistical hurdles, the technical preparation of Amir Ghalenoei will be compromised before the first whistle, leading to a performance deficit that will be visible in the group stage standings.\n\n       Critique:* The prompt's \"Visti\" background is clearly a mistake (Ukrainian gazette). I must ignore it and stick to the \"Visa\" context of the main story.\n       Word count check:* Aiming for 350-400.\n       Tone check:* Is it Davide Longo? Yes. Cynical, focused on the \"meccanismi,\" no \"gladiators.\"\n\n    (Self-Correction during drafting): Make sure not to repeat the \"12 hours\" or \"Amir Ghalenoei\" too much, as they are in Corpo1, but use them to build the analysis.\n\n    Drafting the text:\n    L'ostacolo burocratico imposto dalle autorità 